From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: census the raw trailing storage of ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Companion probe to 0003, for llvm/llvm-project#191361.

Applies on top of 0003 (same function, immediately before the value-init
block, so the census observes the storage as the allocator left it).

Purpose: rate measurements cannot distinguish "MallocPreScribble made the
garbage harmless" from "MallocPreScribble never applied to this
allocation." MallocPreScribble=1 did NOT move the crash rate, which the
uninitialized-trailing-array mechanism says it should have -- an
0xAA-filled array yields an invalid TemplateArgument kind, so
StmtProfiler::VisitTemplateArgument would never reach VisitType. This
patch looks at the bytes directly instead of inferring from rates.

Each ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl created by deserialization has its
trailing array classified as all-zero / all-0xAA / all-0x55 / mixed, and
a single line is printed at exit:

  [ics-census] arrays=N zero=A aa=B 55=C mixed=D sizeof(TemplateArgument)=24 \
      first-mixed-N=2 bytes=0100000010f662d30b00000001000000

Expected, if the mechanism is right:

  stock                 mostly zero, minority mixed (tracks the crash rate)
  reserve(3072)         ~all zero (no rehash, so no dirty block to recycle)
  MallocPreScribble=1   all aa if the knob applies here; unchanged if not
  MallocScribble=1      all 55 if free-fill lands in the recycled slab;
                        all zero would mean the knob suppresses by changing
                        how large frees are recycled, not by neutering the
                        garbage -- which would retire the
                        freed-vs-uninitialized framing entirely

Implementation notes: allocation-free by design (a heap allocation here
would perturb the layout under investigation), so fixed-size statics and
one stack byte. Reporting goes through atexit rather than Sema, so this
patch touches no file other than DeclTemplate.cpp; a crashing run aborts
and prints nothing, which is fine because census runs are successful ones.
The byte-at-a-time memcpy is a deliberate way to read formally
uninitialized storage; it is not a pattern for real code.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of
the llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's
sourceRoot (clang-src-.../clang).
---
diff --git a/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp b/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
index 8744c85..99574a6 100644
--- a/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
+++ b/lib/AST/DeclTemplate.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include "llvm/Support/raw_ostream.h"
 #include <cassert>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <memory>
 #include <optional>
 #include <utility>
@@ -1157,6 +1158,81 @@ ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl::CreateDeserialized(
       new (C, ID, additionalSizeToAlloc<TemplateArgument>(NumTemplateArgs))
           ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl(EmptyShell{}, NumTemplateArgs);
 
+  // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream).
+  //
+  // Census what the trailing storage actually contains, BEFORE anything writes
+  // it. This exists to answer a specific question: do the allocator knobs
+  // (MallocPreScribble / MallocScribble) reach this storage at all? Rate
+  // measurements alone cannot distinguish "the fill made the garbage harmless"
+  // from "the fill never applied to this allocation."
+  //
+  // Reading uninitialized memory is formally UB; the byte-at-a-time memcpy is
+  // the practical way to look at it without inviting the optimizer to reason
+  // about it. Do not copy this pattern into real code.
+  //
+  // Deliberately allocation-free: a heap allocation here would perturb the very
+  // layout under investigation. Fixed-size statics and a stack byte only.
+  //
+  //   CLANG_ICS_CENSUS=1 -> classify each array, report once at exit
+  //
+  // The report is registered with atexit rather than hung off Sema, so this
+  // patch touches no other file. A crashing run aborts and prints nothing --
+  // census runs are meant to be successful ones.
+  if (NumTemplateArgs && std::getenv("CLANG_ICS_CENSUS")) {
+    static unsigned long long Total = 0, Zero = 0, ScribAA = 0, Scrib55 = 0,
+                              Mixed = 0;
+    static unsigned char Sample[24];
+    static unsigned SampleN = 0;
+    static bool Registered = false;
+
+    if (!Registered) {
+      Registered = true;
+      std::atexit([] {
+        llvm::errs() << "[ics-census] arrays=" << Total << " zero=" << Zero
+                     << " aa=" << ScribAA << " 55=" << Scrib55
+                     << " mixed=" << Mixed << " sizeof(TemplateArgument)="
+                     << sizeof(TemplateArgument);
+        if (SampleN) {
+          static const char Hex[] = "0123456789abcdef";
+          llvm::errs() << " first-mixed-N=" << SampleN << " bytes=";
+          for (unsigned I = 0; I != sizeof(Sample); ++I)
+            llvm::errs() << Hex[Sample[I] >> 4] << Hex[Sample[I] & 0xf];
+        }
+        llvm::errs() << "\n";
+      });
+    }
+
+    const auto *Bytes =
+        reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char *>(Result->getTrailingObjects());
+    const size_t NumBytes =
+        size_t(NumTemplateArgs) * sizeof(TemplateArgument);
+
+    bool AllZero = true, AllAA = true, All55 = true;
+    for (size_t I = 0; I != NumBytes; ++I) {
+      unsigned char B;
+      std::memcpy(&B, Bytes + I, 1);
+      AllZero &= (B == 0x00);
+      AllAA &= (B == 0xAA);
+      All55 &= (B == 0x55);
+    }
+
+    ++Total;
+    if (AllZero)
+      ++Zero;
+    else if (AllAA)
+      ++ScribAA;
+    else if (All55)
+      ++Scrib55;
+    else {
+      ++Mixed;
+      if (!SampleN) {
+        std::memcpy(Sample, Bytes,
+                    NumBytes < sizeof(Sample) ? NumBytes : sizeof(Sample));
+        SampleN = NumTemplateArgs;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream).
   //
   // The trailing TemplateArgument array is left as raw storage here; it is
-- 
